HST Office: the colourful HST icon style (hst_modern) is the default; the classic one stays.

Reason: the owner chose the colourful style as default ("Hiện đại (nhiều màu)") with the classic
HST style ("Cổ điển") as an option. Automatic (SymbolStyle "auto") now prefers hst_modern /
hst_modern_dark, then hst / hst_dark. The two values of the options page, "hst_modern" and "hst",
name a style: on a dark UI they select the style's _dark variant. hst_modern* are SVG-only, so
macOS rasterises them at the backing scale like hst*. A colourful glyph not drawn yet falls back
to its classic HST shape, then to the SVG Colibre. configure accepts and installs the two themes
(built by scripts/brand/build-hst-icon-theme.py like hst*); the per-theme raster cache stamp of
hst-icon-theme-hidpi-and-cache.patch covers the new cache directories.

Applies after hst-icon-theme.patch and hst-icon-theme-hidpi-and-cache.patch.
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme, test_IconThemeSelector).
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
